---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const faq = [
	{
		question: 'Is every 2.5 inch fire hose coupling interchangeable?',
		answer: 'No. A nominal 2.5 inch or 65 mm size does not identify the locking or thread pattern. Storz, National, John Morris, Nakajima and instantaneous couplings require the matching mating half or a verified adaptor.'
	},
	{
		question: 'What is a Storz coupling?',
		answer: 'Storz is a symmetric quick-connect coupling. The verified Storz product is a German-standard 2.5 inch aluminum coupling with a self-sealing edge, quarter-turn connection and barbs for layflat hose.'
	},
	{
		question: 'When should I use a hydrant adapter coupling?',
		answer: 'Use an adapter where the hydrant outlet standard and the hose or nozzle standard differ. Confirm both mating interfaces, nominal size, gasket and working pressure; an adapter should solve a defined boundary mismatch, not hide an uncertain hose schedule.'
	},
	{
		question: 'What working pressure should I specify?',
		answer: 'Rate the complete line: hydrant, coupling, hose, nozzle and any adapter. The verified Storz coupling and HS hydrant hose adapter are listed at 1.6 MPa; confirm the exact pressure requirement for the full assembly before ordering.'
	},
	{
		question: 'Should I choose aluminum or brass?',
		answer: 'Aluminum is lightweight and is used for the Storz and HS coupling products in this range. The order should state the required material, finish, gasket and service environment; confirm any brass option or compatibility requirement with the quotation.'
	},
	{
		question: 'What should be in one coupling order?',
		answer: 'Specify the standard by name, nominal size, mating half, hose-tail or thread end, material, gasket, working pressure, hose length and nozzle interface. A sample or dimensional drawing is useful when the local fire department standard is not obvious.'
	}
];

const products = [
	{
		slug: 'storz-coupling-2-5inch-aluminum',
		name: 'Aluminum Storz Fire Coupling (2.5" · German Standard)',
		img: '/assets/products/storz-coupling-2-5inch-aluminum-overlay.png',
		desc: 'German Storz, aluminum, 1.6 MPa, self-sealing, barbed'
	},
	{
		slug: 'fire-hydrant-hose-coupling-adapter-hs',
		name: 'Aluminum Firefighting Hydrant Hose Coupling Adapter (HS Series)',
		img: '/assets/products/fire-hydrant-hose-coupling-adapter-hs.jpg',
		desc: 'DN50 / DN65, 2.5-inch internal thread, 1.6 MPa'
	},
	{
		slug: 'fire-hose-pvc-rubber-lining-8-65',
		name: 'PVC Rubber Lining Layflat Fire Hose (Model 8-65)',
		img: '/assets/products/fire-hose-pvc-rubber-lining-8-65.jpg',
		desc: '19–400 mm inner diameter, standard 65 mm coupling size'
	},
	{
		slug: 'adjustable-pistol-grip-fire-nozzle',
		name: 'Adjustable Pistol Grip Firefighting Nozzle',
		img: '/assets/products/adjustable-pistol-grip-fire-nozzle.jpg',
		desc: '1.5" / 2" / 2.5" inlet, 150–500 LPM, straight to fog'
	}
];
---

<Layout
	title="Storz Coupling & Fire Hose Couplings | Hydrant Adapters | WLFE"
	description="Storz coupling, fire hose coupling and hydrant adapter selection: compare standards, materials, working pressure and hose/nozzle interfaces for B2B orders."
	type="product"
	productData={{
		name: 'Fire Hose Couplings and Hydrant Adapters',
		image: '/assets/products/storz-coupling-2-5inch-aluminum-overlay.png',
		description: 'Fire hose couplings, Storz interfaces, hydrant hose adapters, layflat hose and adjustable nozzles for B2B firefighting line assemblies.'
	}}
	faq={faq}
	breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Fire Hose Couplings' }]}
>
	<main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 mb-16">
		<nav class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-6 flex gap-2"><a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/products/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Products</a><span>/</span><span class="text-gray-600">Fire Hose Couplings</span></nav>

		<article class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-10">
			<p class="text-brand-red font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-sm mb-3">Fire Hose Interfaces — Factory Direct</p>
			<h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 leading-tight tracking-tight">Storz Coupling and Fire Hose Coupling Selection</h1>
			<p class="mt-5 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-lg">A fire hose coupling is only correct when its standard, mating half, gasket, material and pressure match the rest of the line. Wanlian supplies Storz coupling, hydrant adapters, layflat hose and nozzle interfaces for project buyers ordering a complete connection set.</p>

			<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-4">{['Storz Quick Connect', 'Hydrant Adapters', '19–400 mm Hose', '150–500 LPM Nozzle'].map(b => (<div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-xl px-4 py-3 text-center"><span class="text-xs font-black text-brand-blue uppercase tracking-wider">{b}</span></div>))}</div>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">Fire Hose Coupling Products</h2>
			<div class="grid grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">{products.map(p => (<a href={`/products/${p.slug}/`} class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden hover:border-brand-red hover:shadow-md transition"><img src={p.img} alt={p.name} loading="lazy" class="w-full h-28 object-contain bg-white p-2" /><div class="p-3"><p class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-800 group-hover:text-brand-red leading-snug transition-colors">{p.name}</p><p class="text-[10px] text-gray-400 mt-1 line-clamp-2">{p.desc}</p></div></a>))}</div>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">Coupling Standards and Selection Table</h2>
			<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 my-5"><table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-gray-200 text-sm"><thead class="bg-gray-50"><tr><th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Selection point</th><th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">What to confirm</th></tr></thead><tbody class="bg-white divide-y divide-gray-200">
				<tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Storz</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">German Storz quick-connect; the verified product is 2.5 inch with aluminum body, self-sealing edge, barbs and 1.6 MPa pressure.</td></tr>
				<tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">National / John Morris / Nakajima / instantaneous</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Treat each as a distinct interface. Confirm the local fire department pattern and use a verified matching coupling or adapter rather than assuming nominal size is enough.</td></tr>
				<tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Hydrant adapter</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">HS series: DN50 / DN65 size range, 2.5-inch internal thread, anodized aluminum alloy and 1.6 MPa working pressure.</td></tr>
				<tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Hose</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Model 8-65 PVC rubber lining hose: 19–400 mm inner diameter, standard coupling size 65 mm; confirm length, diameter and coupling ends.</td></tr>
				<tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Nozzle</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Adjustable pistol grip nozzle: 1.5", 2" or 2.5" inlet, aluminum alloy, 150–500 LPM and straight-stream to fog patterns.</td></tr>
			</tbody></table></div>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">What to Include in One Coupling Order</h2>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2"><li><strong>Standard and mating half</strong> — Storz, National, John Morris, Nakajima or instantaneous, named explicitly for both ends.</li><li><strong>Size and end configuration</strong> — nominal hose diameter, coupling size, thread or hose-tail, and whether the coupling is loose or factory fitted.</li><li><strong>Material and sealing</strong> — aluminum or other specified material, finish, gasket and service medium such as clear water or foam mixture.</li><li><strong>Complete line match</strong> — hose, adapter, nozzle, working pressure, length and destination fire department interface.</li></ul>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">Fire Hose Coupling Resources</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Read the <a href="/guides/fire-hose-coupling-standards-guide/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">fire hose coupling standards guide</a>, <a href="/guides/fire-hose-buying-guide/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">fire hose buying guide</a> and <a href="/guides/fire-hydrant-valve-standards-guide/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">fire hydrant valve standards guide</a> before releasing a coupling schedule.</p>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-6 tracking-tight">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="space-y-4">{faq.map(item => (<details class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 p-5 open:border-brand-red/30"><summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-bold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer list-none"><span>{item.question}</span><span class="text-brand-blue text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-sm">{item.answer}</p></details>))}</div>

			<div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden"><div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-blue to-blue-800 px-6 sm:px-10 py-10 text-center"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white tracking-tight">Need a Matched Fire Hose Coupling Set?</h2><p class="mt-3 text-blue-100 max-w-xl mx-auto text-sm leading-relaxed">Send the local coupling standard, hose size and nozzle interface — we will confirm the compatible package and reply with a quotation within 12 hours.</p><div class="mt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-center gap-4"><a href="/contact/?product=Fire%20Hose%20Couplings" class="px-8 py-4 bg-brand-red text-white font-bold rounded-lg hover:opacity-90 transition">Request a Quote</a><a href="https://wa.me/8618684324501?text=Hi%2C%20I%20need%20fire%20hose%20couplings" class="px-8 py-4 bg-white text-brand-blue font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-50 transition" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chat on WhatsApp</a></div></div></div>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>
